+# Security Fix: CVE-2026-111497
+
+**Package**: pyarrow 18.1.0
+**CVE**: CVE-2026-111497
+
+## Vulnerability
+
+Out-of-bounds write in the Google Brotli decoder (`c/dec/decode.c`),
+versions 1.0.3 through 1.2.0. pyarrow 18.1.0 statically links the
+Brotli v1.0.9 that Apache Arrow bundles. Those sources are not in the
+PyPI sdist, so a sdist patch cannot fix the CVE.
+
+## Fix
+
+`build/build.sh` clones apache-arrow-18.1.0 and points
+`cpp/thirdparty/versions.txt` at Brotli v1.0.10. That release is v1.0.9
+plus google/brotli commit 50a9b70 and the version bump. The wheel is
+built from that tree with Brotli left enabled.
+
+This file is a marker so patch-source has a diff to apply. It does not
+change the wheel.
+
+## References
+
+- https://github.com/google/brotli/releases/tag/v1.0.10
+- https://github.com/google/brotli/commit/50a9b70a4d5e1443fc40927952276b68fffa83a0
